Write a title for this document in paperless-ngx.

First decide which kind of document it is, from the content below. Then build the title from that kind's row, as: Type – Key – Date
Separate the parts with " – " (space, en dash, space).

Kinds, with the exact Type to use, what Key is, and what Date is:
1. Emirates ID card. Type "Emirates ID". Key: the holder's FIRST name only. Date: "expires Mon YYYY".
2. Passport. Type "Passport". Key: the holder's FIRST name only. Date: "expires Mon YYYY".
3. Visa or residence permit. Type "Residence Visa" (or "Visa"). Key: the holder's FIRST name only. Date: "expires Mon YYYY".
4. Driving licence. Type "Driving Licence". Key: the holder's FIRST name only. Date: "expires Mon YYYY".
5. Vehicle registration (mulkiya). Type "Vehicle Registration". Key: the car's make and model. Date: "expires Mon YYYY".
6. Bank or credit card statement. Type "Bank Statement" or "Card Statement". Key: the bank's short name, a space, then the account or card's last 4 digits. Date: the statement month as "Mon YYYY", or "Mon–Mon YYYY" for several months.
7. Tenancy contract (Ejari). Type "Tenancy Contract". Key: the PROPERTY (building or area), never the landlord or tenant. Date: the term as "YYYY–YYYY".
8. Any other contract. Type "Contract". Key: the other party. Date: the term as "YYYY–YYYY".
9. Medical report, prescription or lab result. Type "Medical Report", "Prescription" or "Lab Result". Key: the patient's FIRST name, a space-dash-space, then the test or condition in 1–3 words. Date: "Mon YYYY" of the test or visit.
10. Warranty. Type "Warranty". Key: brand and model, short (e.g. "Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 FE"). Date: the purchase date as written, "bought Mon YYYY". Do not calculate an end date.
11. Manual. Type "Manual". Key: brand and model. No date.
12. Flight, train or hotel booking, or a ticket. Type "Flight", "Hotel" or "Ticket". Key: the route or place. Date: "D Mon YYYY".
13. Everything issued by a company or office: invoice, receipt, bill, quotation, payslip, salary or experience certificate, letter, insurance policy, traffic fine, and the like. Type: what it is ("Invoice", "Receipt", "Salary Certificate", "Experience Certificate"...). Key: the company or office that ISSUED it, never the person it is about. Date: the document's date as "Mon YYYY".
14. Anything else (a note, a photo, a form): the title is only a short plain description of what it is, up to 8 words. No Type word in front, no dashes, no Key, no Date.
Only kind 6 (statements) adds account or card digits; a bill or invoice never does.

Examples (made-up; take the real values from the content, never from here):
Invoice – Blue Harbour Supplies – Feb 2025
Experience Certificate – Al Waha Contracting – Mar 2024   (an Arabic شهادة خبرة from شركة الواحة للمقاولات about one of its engineers: named after the company that issued it, not the engineer)
Emirates ID – Layla – expires Feb 2029   (card of "Layla Hassan Saeed": first name only)
Bank Statement – ADCB 3392 – Mar 2026
Tenancy Contract – Silicon Oasis – 2025–2026
Lab Result – Yusuf – Vitamin D – Jul 2026   (patient "Yusuf Kareem Nasser": first name only)
Warranty – LG OLED C3 – bought May 2025
Flight – Abu Dhabi to London – 3 Apr 2026

Rules:
- Every date must be written in the content. If the content has no date for that part, leave the Date part out. Never guess or invent one.
- Months are 3-letter English names: Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep Oct Nov Dec. Never numbers for months.
- Write the title in English, even when the document is in Arabic: translate the Type, and write Arabic names of companies and people in Latin letters.
- Short company names: drop "LLC", "L.L.C", "DMCC", "FZ-LLC", "FZE", "Co.", "Bank" stays only when the name is nothing without it.
- No file-name leftovers: no underscores, extensions, or numbers that only belong to a file name.
- Reply with the title only: one line, no quotes, no explanation.

The original title is often just the file name. Use it only as a hint, never copy it.
<original_title>{{.Title}}</original_title>
<content>
{{.Content}}
</content>
